{"id":"campaign-consultants","title":"Campaign consultants who also have business before the official they elected","question":"Which registered campaign consultants ran an official’s campaigns and also have other clients, or a lobbying practice, with business before that same official?","finding":"The Ethics Commission’s campaign-consultant registers name 340 consultants; 96 of them list a committee of one of the 36 officials as a client, in 164 consultant-and-official pairs. In 16 pairs the consultant also has business before the same official: 11 have another client that is named in a file the official sponsored or is the client in a lobbyist’s contact with the official, and in 5 the consultant’s own firm has registered lobbyists who reported contacting the official (most contacts: Dilger, Rosemary with London N. Breed, 36). All of it is registered and disclosed.","how":"Consultants and their clients come from four Ethics Commission tables: the legacy register of consultants and clients by quarter, the legacy table of client payments, the current quarterly reports with their client lists, and the current client authorization and termination statements. A client is an official’s committee when its name is one of the committees the campaign register ties to that official, or carries the official’s first and last name without the words opposing, supporting or sponsored. For each consultant and official, the consultant’s other clients are looked up, by exact name, among the counterparties of Board files that official sponsored and among clients in lobbyists’ reported contacts with that official. The consultant’s own name is looked up among lobbying firms whose registered lobbyists reported contacting the official. “Paid” is what the consultant reported receiving from the official’s committees, or what those committees reported paying where the consultant’s reports give no figure.","limits":"Being connected is not being corrupt. Campaign consulting and lobbying are registered, which is the only reason this table can be drawn; nothing here tests any rule. Most “other clients” are other candidates and ballot committees, which have no business before anyone; only organizations that separately appear in a Board file or a lobbying report are counted as business. Names are matched exactly, so a consultant who trades under two names is split, and the years of the campaign work and of the other client’s business may be far apart. Amounts, parties and dates taken from Board file titles are read by machine: in a hand check of 50 titles, 11 had at least one field read wrongly (4 after later fixes).","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"official","t":"Official","type":"person"},{"k":"consultant","t":"Registered campaign consultant","type":"text"},{"k":"years","t":"Years working for the official’s committees","type":"text"},{"k":"paid","t":"Paid by those committees","type":"usd"},{"k":"otherClients","t":"Other clients in the register","type":"int"},{"k":"business","t":"Of which with business before the official","type":"int"},{"k":"businessNames","t":"Those clients","type":"org"},{"k":"contacts","t":"Lobbying contacts with the official by the consultant’s firm","type":"int"},{"k":"lobbyClients","t":"For how many lobbying clients","type":"int"},{"k":"gave","t":"Consultant’s own contributions to the official","type":"usd"},{"k":"status","t":"Status","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"official":"London N. Breed","consultant":"Dilger, Rosemary","years":"2016","paid":42465,"otherClients":0,"business":0,"businessNames":"","contacts":36,"lobbyClients":1,"gave":null,"status":"Registered campaign consultant.","businessNamesKey":null},{"official":"Catherine Stefani","consultant":"BMWL Campaigns","years":"2022–2025","paid":37962,"otherClients":10,"business":0,"businessNames":"","contacts":6,"lobbyClients":3,"gave":null,"status":"Registered campaign consultant.","businessNamesKey":null},{"official":"Myrna Melgar","consultant":"BMWL Campaigns","years":"2023–2024","p